    <solution><p><alert>A.</alert>
If <m>n = 4</m>, <m>\Delta t = \frac{16-0}{4} = 4</m>.
Thus <m>(t_0, t_1, t_2, t_3, t_4) = (0, 4, 8, 12, 16)</m> and 
<m>(f(t_0), f(t_1), f(t_2), f(t_3), f(t_4)) = (29, 27, 24, 22, 20)</m>.</p>
<p><alert>B.</alert>
The left-hand sum is</p>
<p>left sum 
<m>= 4 (29 + 27 + 24 + 22) = 408.</m></p>
<p>And the right-hand sum is</p>
<p>right sum 
<m>= 4 (27 + 24 + 22 + 20) = 372.</m></p>
<p><alert>C.</alert>
Here, <m>\Delta t = 8</m>, so 
<m>(t_0, t_1, t_2) = (0, 8, 16)</m> and
<m>(f(t_0), f(t_1), f(t_2)) = (29, 24, 20)</m>.</p>
<p><alert>D.</alert>
The left- and right-hand sums are</p>
<p>left sum <m>= 8 (29 + 24) = 424</m>, and</p>
<p>right sum <m>= 8 (24 + 20) = 352</m>, and</p>
</solution>
